---
import '../styles/studio.css';
const examples = [
  {id:'psx-character',name:'PSX · retro adventurer',description:'One full-body character, simple equipment and a readable silhouette.'},
  {id:'psx-world',name:'PSX · game world',description:'Chunky buildings, a clear route through the scene and an elevated game camera.'},
  {id:'psx-prop',name:'PSX · inventory prop',description:'One object in three-quarter view with large details and a plain background.'},
  {id:'anima3d-character',name:'Low Poly · character portrait',description:'A close portrait with angular clothing, a few main colors and one clear accessory.'},
  {id:'anima3d-diorama',name:'Low Poly · miniature diorama',description:'One main structure and a few props on a compact isometric island.'},
  {id:'anima3d-landscape',name:'Low Poly · angular landscape',description:'Faceted terrain, a winding river and distinct foreground and background.'},
];
---
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"/><meta name="description" content="Trained Anima Low Poly styles, guided presets and local examples in Atelier."/><title>Trained Low Poly — Atelier Guide</title></head><body>
<header><a class="brand" href="/studio/">← atelier</a><span>Low Poly guide · October 31, 2026</span></header>
<main style="max-width:1100px;padding-bottom:70px"><section class="intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">TRAINED STYLES. SIMPLE STARTING POINTS.</p><h1>Build a polygon world.</h1><p>Choose a trained Anima Low Poly variant, describe your subject and let a recipe prepare the rest.</p></div></section>
<section class="guide"><div><h2>Choose your look</h2><p><strong>Anima · Low Poly PS1 / PSX</strong> gives characters, game worlds and props a retro console appearance with angular geometry and simple textures.</p><p><strong>Anima · Low Poly Style</strong> aims for stylized game characters, miniature dioramas and landscapes with grouped colors and visible polygon faces.</p></div><div><h3>What the recipe prepares</h3><p>The trained adapter is applied automatically to Anima Aesthetic. Recommended uses 35 Euler steps and CFG 4.5. Draft uses 30 steps at a smaller size; More detail uses 45 steps.</p><p>The PSX trigger is “lowpoly, ps1, psx, low poly, 3d”. Low Poly Style uses “l0wp0ly” with zeros. Guided mode supplies these automatically. Keep the seed fixed while changing a pose, a color or the camera.</p></div><div><h3>Describe a clear subject</h3><p>For a character, name a role, two main clothing colors and one accessory. For a scene, choose one focal building and a clear route through the world. For a prop, use one recognizable object and an uncluttered background.</p><p>Setting and extra details are optional. Only the subject is required. In Free prompt mode, the selected model variant still applies its adapter; add the appropriate trigger words yourself.</p></div></section>
<section aria-labelledby="examples-title"><h2 id="examples-title">Generated here, ready to change</h2><p>These examples use the installed variants. “Try this recipe” restores the recorded example inputs and seed in the studio.</p><div class="recipe-grid">{examples.map(example=><article class="recipe-card"><img src={'/studio/recipe-examples/'+example.id+'.webp'} width="1024" height="1024" loading="lazy" alt={example.name+' generated example'}/><div class="recipe-card-body"><h3>{example.name}</h3><p>{example.description}</p><a class="quiet button" href={'/studio/?recipe='+example.id+'#workspace'}>Try this recipe ↗</a></div></article>)}</div></section>
<section class="guide"><div><h2>When the image misses the mark</h2><p>Reduce the number of props, give the figure a clearer silhouette or simplify the lighting. A stronger composition usually helps more than extra sampling steps.</p><p>Describe one camera angle and a few large color regions. A fixed seed makes small changes easier to compare. The two trained styles have different visual biases; use the example closest to your intended result.</p></div><div><h3>Images and game assets</h3><p>These are image generators. They do not export meshes, UV maps or rigged characters. For modeling references, use a simple pose and an unobstructed three-quarter view. Separate generations do not guarantee consistent front and back views.</p><p>The PNG is an ordinary image at the chosen canvas size. Pixel-grid cleanup belongs to Krea Pixel Art and is not applied to these Low Poly styles.</p></div><div><h3>Versions and sources</h3><p>The installed PSX adapter is Konan’s Preview2 release supplied locally. Low Poly Style is the Anima version by PrettyAIGirls. Both use the existing Anima Aesthetic base weights.</p><p><a href="https://civitai.com/models/2485743?modelVersionId=2794693" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">PS1 / PSX · author and terms ↗</a></p><p><a href="https://civitai.com/models/2204336?modelVersionId=2692813" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Low Poly Style · author and terms ↗</a></p><p><a href="https://huggingface.co/circlestone-labs/Anima/blob/main/LICENSE.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Anima base-model license ↗</a></p><p>The authors allow commercial images under their published creator terms. The CircleStone base-model license also applies.</p></div></section>
</main></body></html>
